  sun: ['Make wudu and pray two rak\'ahs. Salah is a set pause with slow movement and breathing built in.', 'Say the morning and evening adhkar. A fixed routine of protection calms the "what ifs".', 'Read or listen to Surah ad-Duha and ash-Sharh, revealed to comfort the Prophet ﷺ.'],
  psy: [['Slow your breathing', 'Breathe in for 4, out for 6, for two minutes. A longer out-breath tells your nervous system you are safe.'], ['Ground yourself', 'Name 5 things you see, 4 you can feel, 3 you hear, 2 you smell, 1 you taste.'], ['Worry time', 'Write worries down and give them 15 minutes at a set time each day. When one pops up outside that, tell it "later".'], ['Worry tree', 'Ask: can I do something about this? If yes, plan the first step. If no, practise letting it go.'], ['Cut the fuel', 'Less caffeine, less late-night scrolling and news, more daylight and movement.']],
  both: [['Name it in dua: the Prophet ﷺ named hamm (worry about the future) and huzn (sorrow about the past) out loud to Allah.', 'Psychologists call this "affect labelling": putting a feeling into words calms the brain\'s alarm system.', 'Say the hamm wal-huzn dua slowly, naming exactly what you\'re worried about.'], ['"Tie your camel, then trust": do your part, leave the result to Allah.', 'CBT\'s worry tree: act on what you can control, let go of what you can\'t.', 'Write the worry down. Circle what you can do today. Hand the rest to Allah in dua.'], ['Dhikr and salah are set times of calm remembrance.', 'Slow breathing and mindfulness lower anxiety.', 'Breathe out slowly on "SubhanAllah". Try the breathing tool below.']],
